The edge length of the regular tetrahedron is $a,$ so the coordinates of the vertices must satisfy
\begin{align*} (x_1 - x_2)^2 + (y_1 - y_2)^2 + (z_1 - z_2)^2 &= a^2 \\ (x_1 - x_3)^2 + (y_1 - y_3)^2 + (z_1 - z_3)^2 &= a^2 \\ (x_1 - x_4)^2 + (y_1 - y_4)^2 + (z_1 - z_4)^2 &= a^2 \\ (x_2 - x_3)^2 + (y_2 - y_3)^2 + (z_2 - z_3)^2 &= a^2 \\ (x_2 - x_4)^2 + (y_2 - y_4)^2 + (z_2 - z_4)^2 &= a^2 \\ (x_3 - x_4)^2 + (y_3 - y_4)^2 + (z_3 - z_4)^2 &= a^2 \end{align*}
Also, $N = \frac{a^2}{3}.$ Since $a^2$ must be an integer, $a^2 = 3N,$ so $N$ must be divisible by 3.
